  "description": "Open-source oncology knowledge base and decision-support project for tumor-board discussion. A deterministic Python rule engine drafts alternative treatment plans from versioned YAML specifications (an LLM does not select regimens or doses); it ships an Onco Wiki, a Plan Builder, and an MCP server. Reports coverage of 103 diseases, 831 indications, 404 regimens, 321 drugs, 189 algorithms, and 542 sources. Source-cited plan drafts are explicitly for clinician discussion and require verification — the maintainer states the project is early-stage, clinical content may be draft or awaiting review, and technical checks are not clinical validation. MIT-licensed code; specifications and generated content CC-BY-4.0.",
